n the unchanged tree formatCitation returns '<title> (timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' with no blockquote — the received value ends with the symptom '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' — so a contains-family assertion such as expect(result).toContain('> \"Relevant text\"') fails and vitest prints that received string, demonstrating the symptom verbatim in the RED output.","when":"formatCitation is called and takes the unparseable-video_url fallback path (console.warn fires, no timestamp link is built)"},{"given":"the same citation as AC-1 (video_url 'not-a-url', snippet 'Relevant text', start_seconds 10, end_seconds 20, non-empty video_title)","id":"AC-2","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation (exercised via app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts, vitest)","then":"the returned string starts with '- ' and still contains the fallback tail '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' verbatim, with the video title kept as plain text immediately after the marker (not inside a markdown link, so '[Test Video Title](' remains absent). Red proof: on the unchanged tree the returned string begins with the title instead of '- ' — the same marker-less, snippet-less value whose tail is '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' — so the prefix assertion (expect(result.startsWith('- ')).toBe(true) or expect(result).toMatch(/^- /)) is red.","when":"formatCitation is called"},{"given":"a citation with source_type 'dynamous' and an empty lesson_url (''), a non-empty snippet (e.g. 'Test snippet text'), non-empty video_title, start_seconds 10, end_seconds 20","id":"AC-3","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation (exercised via app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts, vitest)","then":"the returned string starts with '- ', contains no '](' (no markdown link is built), and still contains its '> \"Test snippet text\"' blockquote on its own line (newline + two-space continuation indent, as the branch emits today). Red proof: on the unchanged tree this branch returns '<title> — 0:10–0:20\\n  > \"Test snippet text\"' — snippet kept but no '- ' marker — so the prefix assertion is red while the snippet and no-'](' assertions already pass.","when":"formatCitation is called and takes the empty-lesson_url Dynamous fallback branch"},{"given":"a YouTube citation whose video_url is 'https://www.youtube.com/' (parses but has no 'v' parameter), a non-empty snippet, non-empty video_title, start_seconds 10, end_seconds 20","id":"AC-4","seam":"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation (exercised via app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts, vitest)","then":"the returned string is fixed identically to AC-1/AC-2: it starts with '- ', contains the fallback tail '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' verbatim, and contains the '> \"<snippet>\"' blockquote on its own line. Red proof: on the unchanged tree this path returns the same marker-less, snippet-less literal whose tail is '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20'; no existing case asserts the marker or snippet here, so the new prefix and snippet assertions are red.","when":"formatCitation is called and takes the missing-v-param fallback path (the second fallback return, distinct from the new URL catch)"}],"dependencies":[],"invariants":["All 30 current cases in app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts keep passing without modification (issue: 'every current case must keep passing'); the acceptance tests are appended, not substituted.","The console.warn on the unparseable-video_url fallback keeps its exact message '[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link — invalid video_url: \"not-a-url\"' (pinned by the existing test); the missing-v-param path keeps warning as well.","On both fallback paths the video title stays outside a markdown link: the result must not contain '[Test Video Title](' (pinned by existing negative assertions).","formatSources is not modified: it only maps formatCitation and joins with '\\n', so every formatCitation return must be a self-contained '- '-prefixed markdown list item whose blockquote is an indented continuation line ('\\n  > \"snippet\"', two spaces, matching what the complete paths emit today at lines 32/35/58).","The empty/blank/undefined snippet guard at the top of formatCitation still returns ''.","Valid paths are byte-identical to today: YouTube with a parseable 'v' param returns '- [title](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=<id>&t=<start>s) — <range>\\n  > \"<snippet>\"'; Dynamous with a non-empty lesson_url returns '- [title](<lesson_url>) — <range>\\n  > \"<snippet>\"'.","Both fallback return literals (the new URL catch, and URL parses but no 'v' param) are fixed together — they share the same defect and must emit the same shape.","No new or version-changed dependencies; only app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts and app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts may change."],"issue":{"number":49,"title":"fix(export): markdown export drops the transcript snippet when a citation URL cannot be parsed"},"out_of_scope":["Backend, database schema, and any dependency changes.","CitationModal.tsx, Message.tsx, ChatArea.tsx, Sidebar.tsx — in-app citation rendering is untouched.","The valid-URL YouTube path and the valid-lesson_url Dynamous path (their output is pinned as-is by existing tests).","formatTimestamp, the export header, and the filename slug.","formatSources itself — marker ownership stays inside formatCitation; moving it there would double-marker valid entries (investigation H2, rejected).","Restructuring or rewriting the 30 existing test cases beyond appending the new acceptance tests (the assertion-coverage gap the investigation found is separate issue material)."],"risks":["Symptom visibility in the red run: if the first failing acceptance assertion is boolean (e.g. expect(result.startsWith('- ')).toBe(true)), vitest prints 'expected false to be true' and the received value carrying the symptom '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' may never 